content.text:
Yes, the API can batch, and this is where it earns its keep over the DOM approach, which could only ever see the one conversation you had open. There is no single call that exports a whole project (that would be the org export you cannot reach). Batch means enumerate the project's conversations, then loop the per-conversation fetch you already validated. The enumeration is the new part, and it is also the least certain part: only the per-conversation endpoint is confirmed. The conversation-list endpoint, its pagination, and the field that marks which project a conversation belongs to are all inferred, so this needs a discovery pass before the real run, same discipline as the schema check earlier.

Run this first and read the console. It confirms your project's ID, the shape of the list endpoint, and whether conversations even carry a project field to filter on:

```javascript
// discovery — run first, read the console
(async () => {
  const ck = n => (document.cookie.match(new RegExp('(?:^|;\\s*)' + n + '=([^;]+)')) || [])[1];
  const org = decodeURIComponent(ck('lastActiveOrg') || '');
  const get = async p => (await fetch(p, { credentials: 'include' })).json();
  console.log('orgId:', org);
  try {
    const pj = await get(`/api/organizations/${org}/projects`);
    const list = Array.isArray(pj) ? pj : (pj.data || pj.projects || []);
    console.log('projects:', list.map(p => ({ id: p.uuid || p.id, name: p.name || p.title })));
  } catch (e) { console.warn('projects endpoint:', e.message); }
  try {
    const cv = await get(`/api/organizations/${org}/chat_conversations?limit=3`);
    const arr = Array.isArray(cv) ? cv : (cv.data || cv.conversations || []);
    console.log('conv-list shape:', Array.isArray(cv) ? `array(${arr.length})` : Object.keys(cv));
    console.log('first conv item:', arr[0]);
    console.log('project field on item?', arr[0] && (arr[0].project_uuid || arr[0].project_id || arr[0].project));
  } catch (e) { console.warn('conversation list endpoint:', e.message); }
})();
```

If `projects` lists this project with an ID, and the conversation items carry a project field, the batch script below runs unchanged. If the list comes back as a bare array with no project field, it cannot filter and will export every conversation in the org instead, which it warns about rather than doing silently.

